ured; details given about Senator Barack Obama's criticism of Senator John McCain's economic policies and about Governor Sarah Palin's income tax report.  [OBAMA&nbsp- speaks about the economy under President Bush.]  [In Pueblo, Colorado, McCAIN&nbsp- praises Palin for the debate.]  The aftermath of the vice-presidential debate introduced.   (Washington: Wyatt Andrews)  A reality check on what both candidates said in last night's debate presented; excerpts shown from the debate; details given about Palin's claims that Obama tried to raise taxes and about small businesses being taxed, Senator Joe Biden's claims about how McCain voted on taxes and his claims about Obama and Iran and Palin's claims about a new Alaska gas pipeline.  [FactCheck.org director Brooks JACKSON&#134;- speaks about taxes.]   (Studio: Katie Couric)  Report introduced.   (New York: Jeff Greenfield)  The audience's perception of the Biden-Palin debate analyzed; details given about Palin's core strategy.  [In debate, PALIN&nbsp- promises to talk straight to the American people; names dangerous dictators Obama would be willing to meet with.]  CBS News/Knowledge Network poll findings about the view of uncommitted voters about the debate cited.  [In the debate, BIDEN&nbsp- speaks about Al Qaeda in Afghanistan and Pakistan and raising two kids alone.]   (Studio: Katie Couric; Washington: Bob Schieffer)  How Palin did in the debate by not making a blunder, how she did not address some questions and how it was a good night for Biden discussed.   (Studio: Katie Couric, Jeff Greenfield)  How the race will come down to Obama vs. McCain discussed.   (Studio: Katie Couric)  The guests on this week's \"Face the Nation\" listed. ", "segment_duration": 480, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63380.0", "legacy_segment_id": 906707, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, 